      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Question",
        "Answer"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Epigraphy vs. paleography?",
          "Epigraphy: durable media (stone/metal/clay). Paleography: perishable media (papyrus/vellum). Overlap is real."
        ],
        [
          "Why can't we decipher everything?",
          "Need: sign inventory, bilingual text or known language, or statistical foothold. Without these, progress is very slow."
        ],
        [
          "What script type is easiest to decipher?",
          "Alphabetic with bilingual text (Rosetta Stone model). Syllabic next. Logographic hardest."
        ],
        [
          "Are there still undeciphered scripts?",
          "Yes: Indus Valley, Linear A, Proto-Elamite, Rongorongo, others"
        ],
        [
          "Best free Latin corpus?",
          "EDCS (490,000+ entries) or CIL online"
        ],
        [
          "Best free Greek corpus?",
          "PHI Greek Inscriptions (packhum.org)"
        ]
      ]
    },
